Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-29-2000||09:16 PM||||UUUM NO! back in the 60s and 70s that was "cool" but on a Fiero why? You have plenty of downforce on the body to keep it stable and planted at Triple digit speeds. If there is anything you'll have a problem with is the headlight covers poping up.. mine did till i cut a hole in the hood now at 130+ they stay down! I guess I'm just not understanding why you'd want this "rake" if you r worried about tire clearance I was running a 255-40-17 on the back of my car with no scrubbing...  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg</A>    Sorry if this sounds brash, please don't take offense to it i'm just lost as to why you'd want this? ||||reg||1
